Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The decoder and encoder are original implementations written from the VP9
Bitstream & Decoding Process Specification, v0.6 (31 March 2016) and v0.7
(22 February 2017), Google and Argon Design, as published by the WebM
project. They are not translations of, and do not derive from, any other
VP9 encoder's or decoder's source: no implementation's code (libvpx,
FFmpeg's libavcodec or any other) was read, and none was run in testing.
The specification's tables (default and fixed probabilities, scans, the
Pareto table, quantiser lookups, subpixel filter taps, block-size lookups)
are reproduced from it as data; tools/gen_tables.py extracts them from the
PDF and regenerates src/tables.rs identically from either version.

Correctness is checked against the WebM project's public VP9 test vectors —
bitstreams and the MD5s of their decoded frames, published as data for
decoder testing at
https://storage.googleapis.com/downloads.webmproject.org/test_data/libvpx/ —
fourteen of which are included in tests/data (listed in its README).

